  "comment": "The terminal lifecycle in REAL is terminal_committed -> notify_consume_enter -> wake_created (all share jobId). The Elm kernel can only consume these as terminal_registered -> terminal_observed, but terminal_committed lacks ownerId. No three-stage JOB_RUNNING / TERMINAL_AVAILABLE_UNCONSUMED / TERMINAL_CONSUMED distinction is captured in REAL — only two stages (pre/post observation) are captured via notify_consume_enter. The Elm kernel collapses both into one ObservationConsumed state. To distinguish 3 stages would require an additional REAL capture seam event between terminal_committed and notify_consume_enter; not present in frozen evidence."
